    title: 'Respiratory Failure Type 1 and Type 2 — and ARDS',
    short: 'Respiratory failure',
    summary:
      'Type 1 is an OXYGENATION failure with a normal or low CO2. Type 2 is a VENTILATION failure with a raised CO2. The distinction is made on the blood gas and it changes the treatment — because in type 2 the problem is that air is not moving, and more oxygen alone does not move air.',
